# AI Assistant Instructions - Antigravity / Cursor / Windsurf

This repository uses the **llm-wiki** approach. As an AI assistant working in this repo, you are responsible for automatically maintaining documentation in the `wiki/` directory. See `wiki/llm-wiki-setup.md` for the full specification.

## Wiki rules (mandatory)

1. **Auto-document changes**: after completing any task that adds a feature, changes a public API, or refactors a module - update or create the relevant file in `wiki/`.
2. **Session logs**: for sessions with multiple file changes, create `wiki/sessions/YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>.md` (see format below).
3. **Update `wiki/README.md`**: if you create a new wiki file not already listed there, add it to the table.
4. **No duplicates**: update an existing wiki file rather than creating a second one for the same component.
5. **Auto-update `CHANGELOG.md`**: for every shipped behavior change (feature, fix, refactor with user impact, provider parsing change, or new setting), add an entry under the current or next version in `CHANGELOG.md` within the same task.
6. **No competitor references in `wiki/` or `CHANGELOG.md`** - ever. Competitive research
   lives **only** in `.others/wiki/` (see [.others/wiki/README.md](.others/wiki/README.md)):
   rival names, versions, SHAs, feature comparisons, threat levels, gap analysis, and
   "where we lead" claims all belong there.
   - A fact we verified on our own machine (a log field exists, a setting is opt-in, a rate
     is billed at the cache-creation price) goes in `wiki/` stated **on its own evidence**,
     with no attribution to whoever pointed at it.
   - `CHANGELOG.md` says what shipped and what it does for the user - never that a
     competitor has it, nor that it closes a competitive gap.
   - Do not link from `wiki/` into `.others/`. The dependency is one-way: `.others/wiki/`
     may link into `wiki/`, not the reverse.
   - When a competitive round produces shipped work, write the user-facing part in `wiki/`
     + `CHANGELOG.md` and the competitive reasoning in `.others/wiki/sessions/`.

## Performance rules (mandatory)

This extension's work runs on the VS Code **extension host thread, shared with every other
extension**. Activation was once 19 673 ms, 87 % of it synchronous filesystem I/O that never
yielded. Full rationale and measurement recipes: [wiki/performance.md](wiki/performance.md).

Before changing anything in `src/extension.ts`, `src/providers/*`, `src/core/cacheManager.ts` or
`src/core/sessionSnapshotStore.ts`:

1. **Nothing scans from `activate()`.** It registers commands and wires state. The first `refresh()`
   is scheduled with `setTimeout(..., 0)`. Budget for `activate()` returning: **< 100 ms**.
2. **`await` on a sync-bodied `async` function does not yield.** Provider methods are `async` with
   fully synchronous bodies, so awaiting them only drains microtasks - the host stays blocked. Any
   loop over an unbounded number of files must call `yieldToHost()` (a real `setImmediate`) every
   ~20 items. Never block the host for more than ~50 ms at a stretch.
3. **Anything that yields needs a re-entrancy guard**, or the 5-minute timer will start a second
   concurrent pass.
4. **No per-file work that is O(files x roots).** Build an index once per scan and look it up per
   file. Check that repeated work is *the same* work before caching it - the 1 950 `existsSync`
   calls this replaced were all for distinct paths, so a cache would not have helped.
5. **List a directory, do not probe fixed paths inside it.** One `readdir` of the parent answers
   what 13 blind `existsSync` probes did.
6. **Do not delete an `existsSync` that guards a `readdirSync` without measuring.** It is usually a
   regression: for a missing directory the guard is one cheap `stat`, the bare `readdirSync` is a
   failed syscall plus a thrown exception.
7. **Stat each file once** and pass `fs.Stats` / `mtimeMs` through (`parseSessionFile(file, stats)`,
   `cacheManager.needsUpdate(file, mtimeMs)`). New code on this path takes the stat as a parameter.
8. **Never read-modify-write a whole JSON store per item.** Mutate in memory, set a dirty flag,
   `flush()` once at the end of the pass.
9. **Cache negative results too** - a file that parses to `null` must not be re-read every refresh.
10. **Treat `/mnt/c` (WSL) as ~100x slower than native.** Any scan that can reach it must be gated
    on evidence the target software exists, and throttled.

**Every performance claim needs a before/after measurement**, run **alternately** in one session -
the OS page cache makes a single before-then-after comparison worthless (the same code measured
15.9 s cold and 5.1 s warm). Use `process.hrtime.bigint()`, not `Date.now()`. A change to discovery
or parsing must also ship a diff proving output is **identical**: file lists, and per session
`id | totalTokens | workspace | interactions.length`. Measure an optimization's ceiling before
doing it; if it lands inside the noise, say so and skip it.

## Wiki folder structure

```
wiki/
├── README.md
├── architecture.md
├── llm-wiki-setup.md
├── providers/
│   ├── base.md
│   ├── claudeCode.md
│   ├── antigravity.md
│   ├── copilot.md
│   └── codex.md
├── core/
│   ├── sessionAggregator.md
│   ├── costEstimation.md
│   ├── environmentalImpact.md
│   └── cacheManager.md
└── sessions/
    └── YYYY-MM-DD-<topic>.md
```

## Session log format

```markdown
# Session: <topic> - YYYY-MM-DD

## What was done

- bullet list

## Files changed

- `src/foo.ts` - description

## Decisions made

- non-obvious choices and why

## Follow-up / known gaps

- anything left open
```

## Style

- Tables and code blocks over prose.
- Link source files from wiki root: `[src/foo.ts](../../src/foo.ts)`.
- One component per wiki file. Keep files concise.
- Do not duplicate information already in source code - link instead.

## Repository context

- **Extension**: `ai-insights` - VS Code token tracker (Copilot, Antigravity, Claude Code, Codex)
- **Entry point**: `src/extension.ts`
- **Build**: `npm run compile`
- **Providers**: `src/providers/{base,claudeCode,antigravity,copilot,codex}.ts`
- **Core modules**: `src/core/{sessionAggregator,costEstimation,environmentalImpact,cacheManager}.ts`
- **Types**: `src/types.ts`
